# Compiled bytecode. `COPY skills/` takes the whole folder into TWO roots
# inside the image, so without this line a stale `.pyc` travels along and stays.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# The credential is NOT copied by the Dockerfile -- it comes in through the
# ENVIRONMENT, at runtime (`env_file` in compose, or the VM's environment in a
# cloud deploy). It stays out of the build context anyway: the whole context is
# sent to the daemon, and a secret does not need to make that trip.
# plow-agents' `image build` refuses to build if these lines are not here.
plow-credentials
plow-credentials.*

# The house: rules, knowledge, traps, handoff and outside material. None of it
# goes into the image, and keeping it out of the context makes the build lighter.
CLAUDE.md
CONHECIMENTO.md
ARMADILHAS.md
HANDOFF.md
PASSOS.md
LEIA-PRIMEIRO.md
MATERIAL-*.md
handoff/
material-de-fora/
.ai-memory.toml
.claude/
.git/
